[{:db/id 17592186124569 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-49bf02f5-63a7-5afa-b61f-cb52dc9f8048"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-49bf02f5-63a7-5afa-b61f-cb52dc9f8048" :question/id #uuid "49bf02f5-63a7-5afa-b61f-cb52dc9f8048" :question/math-academy-id "q-81738" :question/problem "Find $f(x,y)$ such that $∇f(x,y)=F(x,y),$ where $F(x,y)=(3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\text{ }i+(4-2xy)\\text{ }j.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient of the function $f(x,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n∇f(x,y)=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,i+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,j.\n$$\n\nSince $∇f(x,y)=F(x,y),$ the function $f(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=4-2xy\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =\\int \\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (3{x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{3}-x{y}^{2}+g(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, differentiating the above expression with respect to $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-2xy+{g}^{′}(y).\n$$\n\nTaking $\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=4-2xy$ into account, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2xy+{g}^{′}(y) & =4-2xy \\\\ {g}^{′}(y) & =4 \\\\ g(y) & =4y+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nFinally, substituting $g(y)=4y+C$ into our expression for $f(x,y),$ we get\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={x}^{3}-x{y}^{2}+4y+C.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-23f524e3-bd79-5da0-98c3-54cfe15b71e1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-23f524e3-bd79-5da0-98c3-54cfe15b71e1" :answer-field/id #uuid "23f524e3-bd79-5da0-98c3-54cfe15b71e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3b6c4808-c2a7-5c97-8912-c4f3de3ef57d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c86c75a8-56c7-544d-9bc9-6d9a38de128c" "answer-8d8717c4-00ef-5595-aeca-97e8db51eb3e" "answer-7ebe7055-048b-506e-b0e8-41cb8